<h2 id="guided-workflow">Move from writing to review to export</h2>
<p>The three-step bar stays nearby as you move through the workspace. Add writing opens your input; Word and Google Docs tools offer their own file or paste starting point. Review opens the reading preview and brings it into view. Export takes you to destination choices and the separate review checkbox. The highlighted step records navigation, not completion or a quality score.</p>
<p>After adding an article, choose <strong>Review this article</strong> below the editor, then <strong>Continue to WordPress</strong>, <strong>Continue to HTML source</strong>, or <strong>Continue to Word</strong> below the preview. An unfinished article import takes precedence in these shortcuts: inspect its pending conversion and apply or clear it before using them for the current article. Navigation keeps writing, source notes, selections, export choices, and approval. It never copies, downloads, or publishes.</p>
<p>The bar reports pending imports, file operations, and your current approval choice. Typing changes no focus or scroll position automatically. File-first conversion previews and explicit navigation bring the relevant section into view. The bar becomes static in short windows so it takes less space while you work. The navigation state stays in this tab and is excluded from backups and exports. Save a private backup before leaving.</p>
